Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "AnimalCrossingNight" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 ;
    :description "An animal (dog) suddenly runs into the road in a low-visibility night environment." .

:actor1 a :Actor ;
    :description "Dog running across the vehicle path" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "High probability of collision with an animal moving unpredictably in the vehicle lane." ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 ;
    :confidenceScore "0.92"^^xsd:float .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

Identified Risks for each risk class
Risk 1:
Description: Collision risk with an unpredictable animal (dog) intruding into the vehicle's lane at night, compounded by poor visibility conditions.
Severity Score: 0.75